`saveOwner` is `@Transactional` (read-write); the finders are `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`. Note each service call is its own transaction — the controller method itself is NOT `@Transactional` (only `deleteOwner` is), so the many reads and the single write during a create run in separate transactions.

`ownerRepository` resolves (under the `spring-data-jpa` profile) to `SpringDataOwnerRepository` at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`, which extends Spring Data `Repository<Owner,Integer>`. `save` is the stock Spring Data JPA `save` (persist/merge based on `BaseEntity.isNew()`, i.e. id == null). `findAll`/`findById`/`findByLastName` use the `@Query` definitions there. There is no custom validation/event code in the repository layer.

The persistence side-effect chain on `save`: `Owner` has `@OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER) Set<Pet> pets` (Owner.java lines 109–110), so cascade would persist pets — but the mapper ignores `pets` on create (see below), so a freshly created owner has none.

The controller-side helpers invoked in `createOwner`, quoted (the ones that gate the request or mutate the owner):

```java
private void normalizeAndValidate(Owner owner) {
    if (!normalizeAddress(owner)) {
        throw new RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    String telephone = toE164(owner.getTelephone());
    if (telephone == null) {
        throw new RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    owner.setTelephone(telephone);
    if (isDisposableEmail(owner.getEmail())) {
        throw new RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    if (!owner.isPostcodeValid()) {
        throw new RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() != null
        && owner.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
        throw new RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    LocalDate effectiveDate = owner.getRegistrationDate() != null
        ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : LocalDate.now();
    owner.setRegistrationDate(toBusinessDay(effectiveDate));
}
```

```java
private void checkForConflicts(Owner owner) {
    if (isDuplicateIdentity(owner)) {
        throw new RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    if (isCityAtCapacity(owner.getCity())) {
        throw new RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
}
```

```java
private void assignDerivedAttributes(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold) {
    owner.setMemberId(memberId(owner));
    owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCount(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(isBulkSignup(owner.getRegistrationDate()));
    owner.setCapacityWarning(isCityApproachingCapacity(owner.getCity()));
    owner.setHouseholdSize(householdSize(owner.getHouseholdId()));
    owner.setMembershipLevel(membershipLevel(owner));
    assignPossibleDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold);
    owner.setRiskFlag(isRiskFlagged(owner));
}
```

